# CNAME Template for Custom Domain
# 
# To use a custom domain with GitHub Pages:
# 1. Buy your domain from a registrar (Namecheap, Google Domains, etc.)
# 2. Rename this file from "CNAME.template" to "CNAME" (no extension)
# 3. Replace the example below with YOUR actual domain
# 4. Configure DNS records at your domain registrar (see DEPLOYMENT.md)
# 5. Commit and push to GitHub
# 6. Enable custom domain in GitHub Pages settings
#
# Example (remove this comment and use your domain):
# meyyappanmuthu.com
#
# OR with www subdomain:
# www.meyyappanmuthu.com
#
# DO NOT include http:// or https://
# Just the domain name

